IMPORT prelude

-- Charities Act 1994 (Singapore) -- registration (s 7), the cost of a Commissioner-ordered audit (s 13), cy-pres (ss 19, 20) and
-- disqualification from charity office (s 28).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1994.txt (amendments to
-- Act 25 of 2021).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 14 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a charity's board members
-- and donors meet. Not encoded: the Commissioner and Council, accounting and reports beyond s 13, the protective powers
-- (ss 23 to 27), fund-raising (Part 8), institutions of a public character (Part 9, in regulations), and the Schedule of exempt
-- charities.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Charities Act 1994 -- governance`

§§ `7 -- registration`

-- s 7(8)(a): the governing board of a charity that is neither registered nor excepted must apply to register "within 3 months after
-- its establishment"; (b) a registered charity must notify a change in its governing instruments or particulars, or that it has
-- ceased to exist, "within 7 days". Default -- $10,000 or 3 YEARS, plus $100 a day.
-- (4), (5): the Commissioner MUST refuse or remove registration if it would be contrary to the public interest.
GIVEN `is excepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since establishment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is in default of registration` IF
    (NOT `is excepted`) AND (NOT `is registered`) AND `months since establishment` GREATER THAN 3

GIVEN `days since the change` IS A NUMBER, `notified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is in default of notification` IF
    (NOT `notified`) AND `days since the change` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `13 -- Commissioner-ordered audits`

-- s 13(2): if the required audit has not been done within 10 MONTHS after the financial year ends, the Commissioner may appoint an
-- auditor. (3): the expenses "must be paid (a) by the governing board members of the charity concerned who shall be PERSONALLY
-- LIABLE, JOINTLY AND SEVERALLY", or (b) only so far as that is not practical, from the charity's funds.
GIVEN `months after year end` IS A NUMBER, `audit done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may appoint an auditor for non-compliance` IF
    (NOT `audit done`) AND `months after year end` GREATER THAN 10

GIVEN `practical to recover from the board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`who pays for the Commissioner's auditor` MEANS
    IF `practical to recover from the board` THEN "the board members personally, jointly and severally" ELSE "the charity's funds"

§§ `19, 20 -- cy-pres`

-- s 19(1): a gift may be applied cy-pres where its purposes (a) have been fulfilled, cannot be carried out, or cannot be carried out
-- in the spirit of the gift; (b) use only part of the property; (c) are better served by pooling; (d) refer to an area or class that
-- has ceased to be suitable; or (e) are adequately provided for otherwise, have ceased to be charitable, or have ceased to be an
-- effective use of the property. (4): trustees are under a DUTY to take steps to have the property so applied.
-- s 20(3): money from collecting boxes, lotteries, competitions, entertainments or sales is "CONCLUSIVELY PRESUMED" to belong to
-- donors who cannot be identified -- so it goes cy-pres without any advertisement or inquiry.
DECLARE Circumstance IS ONE OF
    `the purpose has been fulfilled`
    `the purpose is impossible`
    `the purpose uses only part of the gift`
    `the area named has ceased to be suitable`
    `the purpose is now provided by the government`
    `the board prefers a different cause`

GIVEN `the circumstance` IS A Circumstance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gift may be applied cy-pres` IF
    CONSIDER `the circumstance`
    WHEN `the board prefers a different cause` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Source IS ONE OF
    `a collecting box`
    `a charity lottery`
    `a named donor's cheque`

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donors are conclusively presumed unidentifiable` IF
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `a named donor's cheque` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `28 -- disqualification`

-- s 28(1): a person is disqualified from being a governing board member, key officer or trustee of a charity if (a) convicted
-- ANYWHERE of an offence involving dishonesty (fraud, corruption, bribery, deception) or terrorism, terrorism financing or money
-- laundering; (b) an undischarged bankrupt; (c) under an undischarged composition with creditors; or (d) disqualified under the
-- Companies Act. (3): a person under (b) or (d) may still act for a charity that is a COMPANY if they have Companies Act permission.
-- (4): disqualification ends when the conviction is spent, on discharge, or at the end of the period.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `convicted of a dishonesty or terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conviction spent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undischarged composition with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disqualified under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `charity is a company and Companies Act permission held` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified` IF
        (`the person`'s `convicted of a dishonesty or terrorism offence` AND (NOT `the person`'s `conviction spent`))
    OR  `the person`'s `undischarged composition with creditors`
    OR  (    (`the person`'s `undischarged bankrupt` OR `the person`'s `disqualified under the Companies Act`)
         AND (NOT `the person`'s `charity is a company and Companies Act permission held`))
